# 01-codelane-mla-decode.diff
#
# Triton grouped-MLA split-K decode rewrite (_fwd_grouped_kernel_stage1 /
# _fwd_kernel_stage2): bf16 mid_o, wave-floored split target, retuned stage 2,
# natural-K gather with cache hints, one-tile-ahead software pipelining.
#
# Origin:  reference/codelane/final_patch.diff, verbatim. Not my work; carried
#          forward to answer whether the code lane composes with the frozen
#          config. Includes that patch's host-side [overlay] engagement marker.
# Base:    sglang 0.5.15.post1.dev20260723+g6c9fd0adc5,
#          git 0e756912eb3cd8f531f95c17299485b9312b2534
# Apply:   cd /sgl-workspace/sglang && git apply <this file>
#
# Measurement: arm B. 889.683 tok/s (n=5, two servers: cand_s2_r1..r3,
#          cand_s5_r1..r2) against a local baseline of 803.786 tok/s (n=6, two
#          servers: base_s1_r1..r3, base_s4_r1..r3) -> +10.69%.
#          Across-restart noise floor 0.71%.
#          Gate: eval_results/cand_s2_20260820_125449, gsm8k strict-match
#          0.9765 +/- 0.0042, equal to the baseline gate.
#          Engagement: analysis/profiles/cand_s2/kernel_table.txt --
#          _fwd_grouped_kernel_stage1 6.57% + _fwd_kernel_stage2 0.33% of decode
#          GPU time, versus 15.35% for the pair in reference/codelane.
